window.docContents[139].resolve({"/The-formalized-objects/#On-the-triviality-of-inhomogeneous-deformations-of-osp_LPAR_1___2n_RPAR____-a-blueprint--The-formalized-objects":{"contents":"These nodes carry the paper's Appendix A items that are not a numbered statement of the body.\n\nItem P1 (the coordinate presentation is a Lie superalgebra of the stated shape). The\nbracket respects the -grading, is super-skew symmetric, and satisfies the\nsuper-Jacobi identity, for arbitrary homogeneous module elements.\n\nThe presentation of .  is presented as\n on a doubled basis, not constructed. The\npresentation is held accountable by four checks: it restricts to the undeformed bracket on\n, it is super-skew, , and multiplication by  is not\ninjective. The deformed bracket restricts likewise.\n\nThe  consistency check. For one explicitly given datum at , an external\ndescription of the bracket table decodes to exactly the bracket defined internally. This is\na check on a single object, not a statement about a format or a program.\n\n","context":"On the triviality of inhomogeneous deformations of osp(1|2n): a blueprint","header":"4. The formalized objects","id":"/The-formalized-objects/#On-the-triviality-of-inhomogeneous-deformations-of-osp_LPAR_1___2n_RPAR____-a-blueprint--The-formalized-objects"}});